WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:06.300
So I recently came across a story that I thought
was really wild, but also somewhat disturbing

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:08.510
and I wanted to share it with you.

00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:14.630
It's about Johannes Kepler, but it's also
about his elderly mother Katharina, the birth

00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:18.500
of science fiction, and our reluctance to
be open-minded.

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:25.019
Kepler was a great German astronomer from
the 17th century, his name pops up in plenty

00:00:25.019 --> 00:00:28.570
of textbooks today, for his laws of planetary
motion.

00:00:28.570 --> 00:00:34.930
He lived in an era where there was no clear
distinction between astronomy and astrology.

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:41.220
But there was a strong division between astronomy
and physics.

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:47.210
People thought that the planets moved by only
the hand of God, Kepler himself wrote plenty

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:54.380
of horoscopes, but he also became the first
person to combine the map of predicting eclipses

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:56.820
with a physical explanation.

00:00:56.820 --> 00:01:02.810
He showed that the movements we can see can
be explained by physical forces.

00:01:02.810 --> 00:01:09.429
At this time, pretty much everyone believed
incorrectly that the sun revolved around the

00:01:09.429 --> 00:01:13.999
earth, and that the earth was the centre of
the universe.

00:01:13.999 --> 00:01:18.429
It's a fair enough belief because that's what
it feels like.

00:01:18.429 --> 00:01:22.889
So it's easy to see how an uneducated guess
might go wrong.

00:01:22.889 --> 00:01:29.979
But Kepler was an astronomer, and he was starting
to realise that the evidence pointed towards

00:01:29.979 --> 00:01:37.209
a very different conclusion, it pointed towards
the heliocentric model presented by Copernicus,

00:01:37.209 --> 00:01:44.429
where the sun is at the centre of the solar
system, and we revolve around it.

00:01:44.429 --> 00:01:49.709
Kepler was a university student when he learned
about the Copernican theory, and he even wrote

00:01:49.709 --> 00:01:54.600
his dissertation about it, but the uni kept
it kind of hush.

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:59.999
Galileo later wrote to Kepler to confess that
he was also a believer in the Copernican model,

00:01:59.999 --> 00:02:05.679
but he hadn't dared to stand up for it in
public yet, and he wouldn't for another 30

00:02:05.679 --> 00:02:06.679
years.

00:02:06.679 --> 00:02:09.979
You might have heard about how that ended
up for Galileo.

00:02:09.979 --> 00:02:15.840
He was tried before the Catholic Church and
sentenced to spend the rest of his life under

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:17.550
house arrest.

00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:25.450
It was in 1616, that an inquisition declared
heliocentrism to be foolish and absurd, and

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:30.630
to contradict the Holy Scripture, they decided
it was punishable by death.

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:37.011
At the same time as Galileo's trial, Kepler
was rushing to try and save his mother, who

00:02:37.011 --> 00:02:42.620
was facing a trial of her own for an equally
if not more, hated crime, witchcraft.

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:48.950
But all of these events are somewhat connected
in an unexpected way.

00:02:48.950 --> 00:02:56.780
Years earlier, in 1609, Kepler had finished
writing a book called Somnium, or The Dream,

00:02:56.780 --> 00:03:04.140
it is often called one of if not the first
example of science fiction writing, because

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:08.240
of how much hard science it contained.

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:12.420
Before I take a look at the story, I would
like to quickly thank Audible for sponsoring

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:13.810
this video.

00:03:13.810 --> 00:03:20.270
The story that I'm sharing today about Kepler
is one that I read about in the first chapter

00:03:20.270 --> 00:03:23.860
of the book Figuring by Maria Popova.

00:03:23.860 --> 00:03:30.130
It is one of the most poetic retellings of
scientific ideas and of the human search for

00:03:30.130 --> 00:03:31.760
truth and meaning.

