00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:41.780
So here's the story originally written in
Latin.

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:47.940
It starts with Kepler falling asleep, and
he has a dream in which he's reading a book.

00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:53.730
In that book, we have the story of an Icelandic
boy called Duracotus.

00:04:53.730 --> 00:05:00.820
He's 14 years old and his mother makes a living
selling mysterious bags of herbs with mystical

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:02.350
markings on them.

00:05:02.350 --> 00:05:06.169
She sells them to ship captains for good luck.

00:05:06.169 --> 00:05:12.090
One day Duracotus cuts open one of the bags
to see what's inside and spills the contents

00:05:12.090 --> 00:05:13.600
out everywhere.

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:17.180
His mother is really angry with this because
it loses her money.

00:05:17.180 --> 00:05:23.311
So instead she agrees to give her son to the
skipper in place of one of the bags, and they

00:05:23.311 --> 00:05:26.460
take off together and sail to Norway.

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:32.960
On the ocean voyage Duracotus becomes seasick
and so the captain leaves him behind on land

00:05:32.960 --> 00:05:37.889
with instructions to go and deliver something
to the astronomer Tycho Brahe.

00:05:37.889 --> 00:05:43.790
Duracotus ends up becoming a student of the
astronomer and spends five years in his care

00:05:43.790 --> 00:05:46.419
learning how to observe the heavens.

00:05:46.419 --> 00:05:51.730
Take this drawing with a grain of salt because
this book was actually written before Galileo

00:05:51.730 --> 00:05:57.530
pointed the first spyglass at the sky, and
before Kepler himself had ever looked through

00:05:57.530 --> 00:05:58.630
a telescope.

00:05:58.630 --> 00:06:03.730
After a few years Duracotus travels back to
Iceland to meet up with his mother, she's

00:06:03.730 --> 00:06:09.130
happy to hear that he has studied astronomy
and reveals that she too possesses lots of

00:06:09.130 --> 00:06:10.210
knowledge on this topic.

00:06:10.210 --> 00:06:16.310
But then she reveals that the reason she has
this knowledge is because she is able to summon

00:06:16.310 --> 00:06:22.500
up these spirits or daemons, which can move
her anywhere on Earth in an instant.

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:27.949
It turns out this doesn't just include the
Earth though because she summons one of her

00:06:27.949 --> 00:06:29.980
favourite spirits to speak with them.

00:06:29.980 --> 00:06:36.560
The spirit tells them that 50,000 miles up
in the Aether lies the island of Levania,

00:06:36.560 --> 00:06:41.520
which is Earth's moon, the spirits are able
to take humans up to the moon in a journey

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:43.270
of four hours.

00:06:43.270 --> 00:06:49.110
Apparently, the journey is a shock to humans,
so they are sedated with drugs for the trip.

00:06:49.110 --> 00:06:54.530
The spirit describes a trip to the moon and
also talks a lot about the Earth, which is

00:06:54.530 --> 00:06:55.530
called Volva.

00:06:55.530 --> 00:07:01.050
The name is picked carefully to represent
revolution or revolving.

00:07:01.050 --> 00:07:08.330
As for the inhabitants of the moon, they believe
that the Earth rotates around the moon.

00:07:08.330 --> 00:07:14.130
Volva goes through the same phases that we
see the moon go through.

00:07:14.130 --> 00:07:18.770
The moon Levania is also divided into two
hemispheres.

00:07:18.770 --> 00:07:23.860
One is called Privolva, which never sees the
Earth, it is the side of the moon that is

00:07:23.860 --> 00:07:26.380
always locked facing away from us.

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:31.640
And the other hemisphere is Subvolva, which
does see the Earth as their moon.

00:07:31.640 --> 00:07:38.240
A lot of the book is then a very detailed
scientific description of how the Earth would

00:07:38.240 --> 00:07:44.900
look from the moon, how eclipses would look,
the size and orbits of planets, and even some

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:48.070
descriptions of creatures that inhabit the
moon.

00:07:48.070 --> 00:07:53.160
Now at the time this was written the idea
that the moon revolved around the Earth was

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:56.810
actually well known and noncontroversial.

00:07:56.810 --> 00:08:03.520
Kepler is trying to suggest that perhaps our
own certainty about Earth's fixed position

00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:11.080
in space with regards to the sun is just as
misguided as the lunar citizens belief that

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:14.000
the Earth revolves around them.

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:18.490
When you're standing on the moon, and the
ground feels firm and motionless beneath your

00:08:18.490 --> 00:08:25.000
feet, and you see this pale blue dot of the
Earth rising and setting against your horizon,

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:28.810
you can really be convinced in something that's
not true.

00:08:28.810 --> 00:08:34.890
The story was written 300 years before Edwin
Abbott's Flatland, and in that book, we are

00:08:34.890 --> 00:08:41.580
exposed to creatures that live in one dimensional
and two dimensional spaces, and we see how

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:48.510
it is utterly impossible to convince them
that there exists a third dimension.

00:08:48.510 --> 00:08:52.660
In Flatland, the reader is left questioning
whether there must be some obvious fourth

00:08:52.660 --> 00:08:57.500
dimension, that we are also incapable of comprehending.

00:08:57.500 --> 00:09:02.950
Kepler hoped that by seeing the absurdity
of the lunar people's belief that the moon

00:09:02.950 --> 00:09:08.000
was at the centre of the universe, that we
ourselves would have the insight to question

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:11.360
whether that was true for us as well.

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:16.840
He wanted to gently expose more people to
Copernicus's theory of the solar system, but

00:09:16.840 --> 00:09:23.830
he knew it would be too complex and abstract
to just present the scientific facts to a

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:26.080
largely scientifically illiterate public.

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:32.730
Instead, he knew that storytelling was an
amazing way to share science, that still remains

00:09:32.730 --> 00:09:33.820
true today.

00:09:33.820 --> 00:09:39.550
Kepler perhaps knew that "The universe is
made of stories, not atoms."

00:09:39.550 --> 00:09:44.990
It's quite convoluted how Kepler presents
the events as being within a book within a

00:09:44.990 --> 00:09:45.990
dream.

00:09:45.990 --> 00:09:51.720
And it creates quite a lot of distance between
Kepler and what he's writing down.

00:09:51.720 --> 00:09:57.770
Perhaps that is deliberate as a way to be
able to deny and say that these are not necessarily

00:09:57.770 --> 00:09:58.770
things that he believes.

00:09:58.770 --> 00:10:02.610
The old fashioned 'retweets are not endorsements'.

00:10:02.610 --> 00:10:09.410
It was called The Dream, but the story was
supposed to awaken people to a new scientific

00:10:09.410 --> 00:10:10.410
truth.

00:10:10.410 --> 00:10:16.440
However, it turned out their society was in
a slumber too deep to be helped.

00:10:16.440 --> 00:10:23.720
Sometime in 1611, the manuscript got leaked,
but the science and symbolism were lost on

00:10:23.720 --> 00:10:29.370
the illiterate, superstitious and vengeful
villages of Kepler's hometown.

00:10:29.370 --> 00:10:35.790
It was taken to be more of an autobiography
since there were a few facts hard to ignore.

00:10:35.790 --> 00:10:42.810
It was well known that Kepler himself had
been an apprentice of Tycho Brahe and Kepler's

00:10:42.810 --> 00:10:46.830
mother was a herb doctor, just like the mother
figure in the story.

00:10:46.830 --> 00:10:53.350
So when their fictional mother character conjoined
up spirits to travel to the moon, that was

00:10:53.350 --> 00:10:54.380
taken literally.

00:10:54.380 --> 00:11:00.529
So apparently a local woman who was already
angry at Katharina over a private matter,

00:11:00.529 --> 00:11:07.670
heard of the book and used it as ammunition
to convince 24 others in the town to testify

00:11:07.670 --> 00:11:10.500
that Katharina was a witch.

00:11:10.500 --> 00:11:16.450
These accounts were as random as a man dating
the onset of his disability to a night 10

00:11:16.450 --> 00:11:22.820
years earlier when he had taken a single sip
from a cup at Katharina's house.

00:11:22.820 --> 00:11:29.330
Kepler took on his mother's legal defence
and dedicated six years of his life to disproving

00:11:29.330 --> 00:11:36.330
each of these allegations, using science to
point to natural causes behind each one.

00:11:36.330 --> 00:11:41.640
But his mother was arrested and taken from
her home in the middle of the night.

00:11:41.640 --> 00:11:48.310
The accounts I've read and say that the dream
wasn't presented as evidence at the trial,

00:11:48.310 --> 00:11:55.590
but Kepler did hold himself at least partially
responsible for her fate having written it.

00:11:55.590 --> 00:12:02.010
Katharina was imprisoned for 14 months and
threatened with torture but confessed nothing.

00:12:02.010 --> 00:12:07.060
Eventually she was released but never recovered
and died not long after.

00:12:07.060 --> 00:12:14.940
Kepler spent the rest of his life obsessively
annotating the dream with 223 footnotes, as

00:12:14.940 --> 00:12:22.310
long as the story itself, his intention was
to dispel superstitious interpretations by

00:12:22.310 --> 00:12:28.020
giving his exact scientific reasons for using
each symbol and metaphor.

00:12:28.020 --> 00:12:33.100
He says in footnote number eight, "if any
of you have read this little book before,

00:12:33.100 --> 00:12:37.339
you will understand what forebodings this
book brought me".

00:12:37.339 --> 00:12:43.610
He says, "These words were taken up by senseless
spirits and finally burned forth into rumour,

00:12:43.610 --> 00:12:47.339
blown up by ignorance and inexperience."

00:12:47.339 --> 00:12:52.240
He takes particular care with describing the
spirits in the book, and in footnote 34 he

00:12:52.240 --> 00:12:58.230
says that they are the spirits of science,
to whom the causes of things are known.

00:12:58.230 --> 00:13:04.800
There are nine of them, metaphysics, physics,
ethics, astronomy, astrology, optics, music,

00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:05.910
geometry and arithmetic.

00:13:05.910 --> 00:13:09.560
He also talks about his ideas of gravity.

00:13:09.560 --> 00:13:13.570
And keep in mind this is before Newton is
even born.

00:13:13.570 --> 00:13:21.440
Footnote 66 says, "I define gravity as a power
similar to magnetic force and mutual attraction.

00:13:21.440 --> 00:13:27.080
The force of this attraction is greater in
bodies close to each other, rather than in

00:13:27.080 --> 00:13:28.360
those that are remote.

00:13:28.360 --> 00:13:33.730
As a consequence, they rather resist separation
from one another when they are still close

00:13:33.730 --> 00:13:35.180
to each other."

00:13:35.180 --> 00:13:40.220
In the very next footnote, he demonstrates
an intuitive understanding of inertia.

00:13:40.220 --> 00:13:45.220
Again, this is before Newton would pen it
down in one of his laws.

00:13:45.220 --> 00:13:50.660
Kepler says "because bodies are heavy, they
resist motion."

00:13:50.660 --> 00:13:56.390
Kepler tried to publish the dream in 1629,
but he ran out of money.

00:13:56.390 --> 00:14:02.170
He travelled 100 kilometres on a horse to
repay debts and try to sell his assets to

00:14:02.170 --> 00:14:03.320
finish printing the book.

00:14:03.320 --> 00:14:09.540
But on his journey, he came down with an illness
and died in 1630.

00:14:09.540 --> 00:14:13.880
The Dream was published in 1634 by Kepler's
son Ludwig.

00:14:13.880 --> 00:14:20.643
For Kepler, it seems that his search for truth
came at a great personal cost.

00:14:20.643 --> 00:14:25.950
The idea that the earth was not the centre
of the universe was the first major challenge

00:14:25.950 --> 00:14:31.640
to our self-importance, and each challenge
since has faced similar resistance.

00:14:31.640 --> 00:14:39.111
300 years later, we would use Kepler's laws
to calculate a trajectory to the moon and

00:14:39.111 --> 00:14:44.340
land there, allowing Kepler's Dream to come
true.

00:14:44.340 --> 00:14:49.029
Thanks for watching this video and thanks
to my Patreon supporters for making it possible.

00:14:49.029 --> 00:14:53.509
A special shout out to today's Patron Cat
